  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Csp 302.01 Separate Account Requirement. The trust documents shall require the establishment and maintenance of a separate account for a participant’s holdings on behalf of a designated beneficiary. Upon acceptance of a completed and executed participation agreement, the trustee shall establish, or shall cause to be established, an account that will be controlled by the participant for the benefit of the designated beneficiary and credit such account with the contributions made by the participant.\n\nSource. #7083, eff 8-26-99, EXPIRED: 8-26-07\n\nNew. #9585, eff 11-2-09; ss by #11097, eff 5-17-16; ss by #13302, eff 12-10-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/csp100-700.html"
